# Private same-level GUI/capture reproduction proposal

Source-only candidate [a1-l3-gui-capture-repro.gd.txt](a1-l3-gui-capture-repro.gd.txt), SHA256 `9d5d1f54edbb063d43c316d4da3eac9ce9370ec9d8267ad56e0bf71a586a76a0` (232 lines). Read baseline `ea99aa49c8ba772f0d96fcff60b1d296ab2f345a`. No parsing, import, native execution, promotion, tracked edits or new UID occurred. Root owns selection, promotion and engine jobs.

Integration [RESPONSE b30499c9](</Users/howardchen/Documents/ChatGPT/video game idea/.cinder/agent-chat/cinder-campaign/integration/messages/b30499c9-75b0-4ee9-91b9-e8f87c5b35db-RESPONSE.json>) SHA256 `e5a658eaca1e4bf2dc26a0a59fbb904f56b7506a5f886631b33bf0c416c2a0b0`, publication `fc4031324db0ae16e8a7c06e1f6144bcf00e5e27` / API38, supplies the diagnostic plan; this proposal does not establish a shared cause or adopt that publication. Original failed1140/1 and all408 frozen origins remain untouched.

The fixture extends the actual current normal full-route test only to reuse its real MainScene/Player/HUD/camera and strict current-containment/deferred-pause/capture helpers. `_run` performs three fixed fresh-spawn loops on `res://scenes/acts/act1/a1_l3_route_greybox.tscn`. It does not invoke the five-room route, move the Hero, activate sources, forge progress or seed actor/profile/HP/ammo/clock state. The inherited `_open_world` includes its existing public rejected premature checkpoint/completion/contact probes and exactly one initial public preview resume; these are setup checks, not earned progression. All nineteen actual sources must remain pristine dormant and no field/encounter is installed. A successful narrow run would not reproduce or disprove the earned Crossed failure.

Each loop uses unchanged `_full_quiet_capture` / `_capture`: the same single2-native-second joint current-view/public deferred-pause window, strict after-pause framing, public HUD hide → existing actual render frame → public HUD show_pause, then actual GUI click. The GUI override keeps the original visible-Button/paused assertion, literal mouse press parse → existing process frame → literal release parse → existing process frame, and exact original three-condition assertion. No buffered-event flush, added click-frame yield, layout wait, sleep, retry-resume, focus request, notification suppression, margin/deadline relaxation or shared edit is proposed. The narrow wall watchdog reuses the existing70-second component bound. Game capture CLI flags are rejected because its current `_notification` would otherwise bypass normal focus handling; this fixture renders through `--script`, not those flags.

Before press, immediately after each parse and after each existing frame, receipts retain monotonic microseconds/process+physics frames, actual paused/public pending state, all three predicate operands, complete detached input/history values and ExactJson scalar bits/types, actual Button ID as string/rect/center/viewport/visibility/enabled/process/mouse-filter/action-mode/pressed-property/draw-mode, HUD mode/shade, actual Game/level/Hero/camera/Window identities and native focus views. Native equality still compares the original native Vector2/Vector3-containing Dictionaries/Arrays; detached vector-component arrays are transport only. The input anchor native type is recorded. All receipts are bounded512; overflow makes the run fail instead of granting incomplete evidence. Signals collect in memory; no stdout logging is inserted between input frames.

Passive later connections to the same actual Button observe gui_input/down/up/pressed and HUD start_requested. HUD/Game setup already connects the native resume path first, so the later HUD receipt samples the actual callback result; it neither emits signals nor invokes Resume. An always-process sibling observer records delivered application/window focus/pause notifications and observed pause/pending/focus transitions. Native root Window focus_entered/exited are separately observed. It reads state and appends private data only. Notification/tick ordering is observed, not assumed to establish exact Game callback order; one per-tick transition sample can miss a same-tick round trip, while the five boundaries and actual signal callbacks retain immediate states. HUD `_mode`/`_shade` and `_card_button` are read-only source-proven fields without public getters.

Interpretation stays conditional: absent pressed points to event delivery/hit/focus; start_requested with pending pause points to the existing resume guard; callback unpaused then final paused demonstrates later re-pause; changed input/history identifies consumption. The fixture does not auto-repair any case, assert an unobserved source or replace Game focus behavior. Existing same-level camera containment stays sovereign. No saves, role combat, finite-spore behavior, five-room floor/art acceptance, legal-kit/public-profile matrix, human testing or performance inference is added. Cleanup clears the actual public PixelEffects, exits/frees the world, and uses the existing one process-frame teardown pattern; no diagnostic timer is added.

Official primary API inspected: [Window4.7](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/classes/class_window.html) Signals focus_entered/focus_exited and const has_focus/get_window_id support passive observations only. [BaseButton4.7](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/classes/class_basebutton.html) Signals button_down/button_up/pressed, ActionMode press/release and get_draw_mode distinguish delivery from a sampled pressed property. [Node4.7](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/classes/class_node.html#class-node-constant-notification-application-focus-out) Notifications WM_WINDOW_FOCUS_IN/OUT and APPLICATION_FOCUS_IN/OUT/PAUSED/RESUMED describe observed OS notifications; paused/resumed platform delivery is not guaranteed on this Mac. No video was accessed.

Root-run suggestion only after explicit promotion to a new owned test path: `python3 scripts/dev/dev.py engine --path . --resolution 540x1170 --script tests/acts/act1/a1_l3_gui_capture_repro.gd` (no `--capture` flags). Parent may choose fewer loops without changing the two input frames/predicate; this draft fixes3. Nothing has been run. Source static checks verified two parses/two existing frame awaits in the click method, the exact original final predicate, no forbidden intervention call, existing resource references and scoped paths; they are not a GDScript parser result.

